---
title: "Packages and extensions available"
flm:
  use: [flmdoc]
  math: false
---
The packages and extensions a document may use: those compiled into the program, those found on the search path, and those bundled into the program.

\section*{Compiled into the program}

The packages compiled into the program:

\begin{itemize}
\item \verbcode{math-passthrough}
\item \verbcode{std}
\end{itemize}

\section*{Found on the search path}

The extensions found in the folders of the search path:

\begin{itemize}
\item \verbcode{narrow}
\end{itemize}

\section*{Bundled into the program}

The extensions bundled into the program:

\begin{itemize}
\item \verbcode{flmdoc}
\item \verbcode{profile-pdf-latex}
\end{itemize}

\section*{Profiles}

A package or an extension whose name begins with \verbcode{profile-} provides the packages of the profile named by the rest:

\begin{itemize}
\item \verbcode{profile-pdf-latex} provides the profile \verbcode{pdf-latex}
\end{itemize}

